1
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:04,140
-早上好呀 先生们 -早
- Good morning, gentlemen. - Hi.

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:05,056
麦克斯 你睡得好吗
Max, how'd you sleep?

3
00:00:05,056 --> 00:00:07,715
我好喜欢在这儿过夜啊
Oh, I love crashing here!

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,220
仿佛回到了大学时代
This is just like college --

5
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:12,080
熬夜到很晚 昏睡在沙发上
staying up too late, passing out on the couch,

6
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,100
走廊上有毒舌的亚洲女
mean Asian chick down the hall.

7
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:15,478
是啊 莉莉人呢
Yeah. Where is Lily?

8
00:00:15,478 --> 00:00:17,280
我不知道 去上学了吧
I don't know. S-School, maybe?

9
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,380
我在这儿呢
I'm right here.

10
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:22,820
我们以前在阿姆斯特丹认识了麦克斯
We met Max in Amsterdam on what we thought

11
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:25,540
本来是一趟陶艺[大麻]咖啡厅之旅 所以...
was a tour of pottery cafes, so...

12
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:26,960
很多事我都不记得了
I don't remember much about it,

13
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:27,900
但我清楚记得
but I do remember thinking

14
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,640
我当时觉得他是我遇过最好笑的人
he was the funniest person I've ever met.

15
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:32,220
我们跟他说 要是来我们这儿
And we told him if he ever came into town,

16
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:33,639
必须住咱们家
that he had to stay with us.

17
00:00:33,639 --> 00:00:35,673
他答应了 我真的好开心
And I-I-I'm so glad he said yes

18
00:00:35,673 --> 00:00:38,020
因为我记得当时一直很神经紧张
because I remember being really, uh, paranoid

19
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:39,020
觉得他不喜欢我
that he didn't like me.

20
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,800
你们俩让开
You two, get out of here.

21
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:43,300
我来煮早餐给大家吃
I'm gonna whip us up some breakfast.

22
00:00:46,548 --> 00:00:48,881
我的头像兴登堡号一样 痛到炸裂
Whoo! My head feels like the Hindenburg.

23
00:00:49,518 --> 00:00:51,348
少来了
Oh, come on!

24
00:00:52,314 --> 00:00:54,709
-怎么感觉他在欧洲时比较好笑 -对
- I feel like he was funnier in Europe. - Yeah.

25
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:57,160
米奇尔 快看
Mitchell! Look!

26
00:00:57,160 --> 00:00:59,145
我们巨贵的那瓶红酒吗
Our crazy-expensive bottle of wine?

27
00:00:59,145 --> 00:01:01,860
我们一直想留到最特别的日子才打开的
I -- uh, we were saving this for the perfect occasion.

28
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:04,680
他一定是等我们睡了 再自己喝掉的
Okay, well, he must've drank it after we went to bed.

29
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:05,425
谁会这么贱啊
Who does that?

30
00:01:05,425 --> 00:01:06,520
不过问主人家
Just drinks somebody's

31
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:08,040
就擅自喝掉别人最贵的红酒
most expensive bottle of wine without asking?

32
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:10,880
-这是仇恨犯罪 -这怎么会是仇恨犯罪
- Okay, it's a hate crime. - How is it a hate crime?

33
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:12,040
因为我恨他
Because I hate him.

34
00:01:12,578 --> 00:01:14,580
真不敢相信都快被他喝光了
I ca-- I can't believe it's almost gone.

35
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,740
我至今只考虑过打开这瓶酒两次
Look, you know, I've only ever considered opening that twice --

36
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,140
一次是大选之夜刚开始
once early on election night

37
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:19,900
另一次是我们以为《爱乐之城》得到了最佳影片奖
and then when we thought "La La Land" won Best Picture.

38
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:21,000
我知道 这一年很不好过
I know. It's been a rough year.

39
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:21,920
吃早餐啦
Breakfast!

40
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:26,060
不 不要啊
No, no.

41
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:27,240
那是我们的鱼子酱吗
Is that our caviar?

42
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:29,160
是啊 幸好我找到了
Yeah! Lucky I found it.

43
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:30,620
被藏在冰箱深处呢
It was hiding in the back of the fridge.

44
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:32,120
因为要留到特别的日子才吃
For a special occasion.

45
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:33,060
有什么问题吗
Something wrong?

46
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:34,240
有 有问题
Yeah... yeah.

47
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:36,460
首先你擅自开了我们价值四百块的红酒
Uh, first you open up our $400 bottle of wine,

48
00:01:36,460 --> 00:01:38,920
现在又开了一罐两百块的鱼子酱
now it's our $200 tin of caviar.

49
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:40,520
-这都是我们特意留起来的 -留着干嘛
- We were saving those. - For what?

50
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:41,780
等到庆祝的时候才享用
A celebration, like --

51
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:43,480
那《月光男孩》得了奥斯卡那次怎么没开
What about when "Moonlight" won the Oscar?

52
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,760
那次对我们群体来说 确实是重要的时刻
Okay, it was a big moment for the community, yes --

53
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:48,620
这样吧 我还是走吧
Okay, you know what? Look. I'm gonna go, okay?

54
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:51,599
但听我一句劝 千万别延迟享受人生
But, guys, don't defer enjoyment,

55
00:01:51,599 --> 00:01:54,200
因为人有旦夕祸福
'cause you never know when you're gonna bite it.

56
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:57,300
要我说 好好享受每一晚
I say, make every night special.

57
00:01:57,541 --> 00:02:00,020
好吧 你这套哲学挺有意思的
Okay, well, that's a -- that's a fun philosophy,

58
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,550
但不是每个人能身体力行 好吗
but not everyone can follow that, okay?

59
00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:03,321
因为我们有责任在身
'Cause -- 'Cause we have responsibilities.

60
00:02:03,321 --> 00:02:04,640
我们有预算
We have -- We have budgets.

61
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:05,920
我们有个女儿
We have a daughter, you know.

62
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:07,060
我们女儿人呢
Where is our daughter?

63
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:09,020
-我不知道 在后院吧 -可能吧
- I don't know. Backyard, maybe? - Maybe.

64
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:22,859
厄尔·钱伯斯
Earl Chambers,

65
00:02:22,859 --> 00:02:26,280
我昔日的生意搭档 后来变成我的死对头
my former business partner-turned dumbass nemesis,

66
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,136
他买了横向衣柜
bought the old horizontal wardrobe.

67
00:02:28,136 --> 00:02:31,140
给你们衣柜业门外汉解释一下 就是他挂了
For you closet non-pros, that means he died.

68
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:34,800
然后在上周 我收到了这个骨灰瓮和这封信
Then last week, I received this urn and this note.

69
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:37,180
"你知道该如何处置我的骨灰
"You know what to do with my ashes.

70
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:38,620
沿着路一直走"
Follow the path."

71
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,120
这是什么鬼意思
What the hell does that mean?

72
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:44,180
你以为可以把我逼疯 但你想都别想
You think you can drive me nuts, but you can't.

73
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:46,640
他听不见你说话的 除非你把盖子打开
He can't actually hear you unless you open the lid.

74
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:47,820
我还是没想明白
I still can't figure out

75
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:48,828
"沿着路一直走"是什么意思
the meaning of "Follow the path!"

76
00:02:48,828 --> 00:02:50,380
我要你帮我打给雪儿
I'm gonna need you to call Shirl

77
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:52,460
搞清楚她爸到底为什么要折磨我
and find out why her father's been torturing me.

78
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,099
-你自己打给她 -你没得选择
- You call her! - That's not an option.

79
00:02:54,099 --> 00:02:56,680
她是个油腻的小滑头 跟她爹一个样
She's a greasy slimebucket, just like her father,

80
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,240
而且不知为何 她不喜欢我
and for some reason, she doesn't like me.

81
00:02:58,748 --> 00:03:00,518
我想想办法吧
Hmm...I'll see what I can do.

82
00:03:09,335 --> 00:03:11,460
曼尼 怎么啦
Hey, Manny! What's up?

83
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,777
你没看到我 一切都很好
I'm not here! Everything's fine!

84
00:03:12,777 --> 00:03:15,620
-超级好 -好吧 我招了
- Super-dupes. - Okay, I'll -- I'll -- I'll talk.

85
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:18,200
昨晚我和卢克到一片不太安全的社区吃玉米卷
Luke and I went to a sketchy neighborhood for tacos last night,

86
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:20,440
然后他不见了 之后我再也没看见过他
and he disappeared, and I haven't seen him since.

87
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:22,100
什么 你最后一次看到他是在哪
What? Where did you see him last?

88
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,340
他跟一个姑娘走了
He went off with this girl.

89
00:03:23,340 --> 00:03:24,873
-跟一个姑娘吗 -是的
- With a girl? - Yeah.

90
00:03:25,563 --> 00:03:26,600
曼尼
Manny.

91
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:28,680
让我告诉你邓菲家男儿的特质
Let me tell you a little something about Dunphy men.

92
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,480
当我们遇到女性时
When we come into contact with a lady,

93
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:32,400
总会给她留下炙热灼烧感[性病]
we leave her with a burning sensation.

94
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:33,300
这么说有点歧义
Let me try that again.

95
00:03:34,382 --> 00:03:36,602
当邓菲男儿遇见性感小妞时
Um...when a Dunphy man sees a sexy skirt,

96
00:03:36,602 --> 00:03:37,940
他就必须"深入"她心房
he's just gotta get in it.

97
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:39,020
-不妥 -我懂你意思
- No! - I get the point.

98
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,900
我很庆幸你是来跟我说
Look, I'm just glad you came to me...

99
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:42,339
我才没有 刚好被你逮到而已
I didn't. You caught me here.

100
00:03:42,339 --> 00:03:44,440
因为我不想克莱尔知道后慌张失控
...'cause I don't want Claire freaking out about this.

101
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:47,034
卢克的电话转到语音信箱了
Luke's phone is going straight to voicemail.

102
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,160
有人在数码门把手上挂了袜子哦
Someone's got a sock on the digital doorknob.

103
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:52,540
我真的觉得你该担心一下
I really think you should be a little worried about this.

104
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:53,100
担心
Worried?!

105
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,160
让我告诉你邓菲家男儿的特质
Let me tell you something about Dunphy men.

106
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,380
菲尔 那一区龙蛇混杂 很不安全
Phil, this was a pretty rough neighborhood.

107
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:58,440
这样吧
Tell you what,

108
00:03:58,480 --> 00:03:59,600
如果能让你放心些
if it makes you feel better,

109
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:01,378
我们一起去那里找找他
we'll go down there and look around for him.

110
00:04:01,378 --> 00:04:04,437
我们需要支援 强有力的支援
We're gonna need backup -- serious backup.

111
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,360
好了 淡定
Okay, be cool.

112
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:08,760
我以前就住在这一区
I used to live in this neighborhood.

113
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:11,740
只要表现得强悍 就没人敢惹你
If you act tough, nobody will mess with you.

114
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:16,639
你们想尝尝
Would you like to try

115
00:04:16,639 --> 00:04:19,000
人道的碱水刨冰吗
a cruelty-free alkaline-water snow cone?

116
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,320
-什么 -免费品尝
- What? - Free sample.

117
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:21,916
去我们的店里有大份的
You can get a larger one down at our stand.

118
00:04:21,916 --> 00:04:23,440
我们还提供翻修乐器大号的服务
We also refurbish tubas.

119
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,440
不用 谢谢
No, thank you.

120
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,280
我的街区怎么了
What happened to my neighborhood?

121
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:28,340
祝你们今天愉快
Have the best day.

122
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:32,160
留络腮胡的白人毁了一切
White people with beards -- they ruined everything.

123
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:35,000
你为什么要说这里危险
Why would you even say that this place was dangerous?

124
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:37,660
晚上这里可怕多了 还放着爵士乐呢
It was a lot scarier at dark. There was jazz.

125
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,160
卢克还是不接电话
Luke's still not answering.

126
00:04:41,207 --> 00:04:42,822
我们会找到他的 菲尔
We're gonna find him, Phil.

127
00:04:42,822 --> 00:04:45,060
我不担心 我经历过
Oh, I-I'm not worried. I've been there.

128
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:47,020
遇见一个女孩 忘了地点和时间
Meet a girl, you lose track of place and time,

129
00:04:47,031 --> 00:04:48,880
不仅是因为你的罗盘表不见了
not just 'cause your compass watch is missing,

130
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:50,880
结果她表哥罗德尼突然也有了同一块表
and suddenly her cousin Rodney has the exact same watch

131
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,038
他还发誓他有那表很久了
but swears it was always his.

132
00:04:52,038 --> 00:04:54,540
瞧瞧 马里奥的汽修店
Oh, look! Mario's Bodyshop.

133
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:56,800
至少有一样东西还没变
At least one thing is still the same.

134
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:58,860
这条街上发生的一切
There's nothing that happens in this street

135
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:00,420
地头蛇马里奥全都了如指掌
that Mario doesn't know about.

136
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:01,580
我们过去吧
Let's go over there.

137
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:06,060
红灯闪烁 警报响个不停
So, red lights are flashing, alarms are blaring.

138
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:09,480
还有大概十秒钟反应堆就要熔毁了 温度高到
We're about 10 seconds from a meltdown so hot

139
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:12,500
会将比利时烧成一汪热巧克力
it's gonna turn Belgium into a pool of hot chocolate.

140
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,130
我突然意识到
And I suddenly realize,

141
00:05:14,130 --> 00:05:17,460
他们没有正确地计算相对扭曲...
they haven't properly accounted for the relativistic distort--

142
00:05:17,460 --> 00:05:18,458
这栋楼是几号楼
Hey, what's this building's number?

143
00:05:18,458 --> 00:05:19,948
我想叫杯思慕雪外送
I'm trying to Postmates a smoothie.

144
00:05:19,948 --> 00:05:21,980
我迅速在脑海中进行了
I quickly do a few multi-dimensional

145
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:23,940
一些多维张量计算
tensor calculations in my head,

146
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:26,280
我将吓哭的警卫推到一边
I push this crying guard to one side

147
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:27,720
调整了同步加速器
and adjust the synchrotron.

148
00:05:28,380 --> 00:05:30,000
我抬头看着倒计时钟
I look up at the countdown clock.

149
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:38,740
你 拿着电话的
You, with the phone!

150
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:41,120
-你叫什么 -艾丽克斯·邓菲
- What's your name? - Alex Dunphy.

151
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:43,948
邓菲女士 我拯救世界
Ms. Dunphy, is my story of saving the world

152
00:05:43,948 --> 00:05:48,007
同时意外创造三种新元素的故事让你觉得无聊吗
whilst accidently creating three new elements boring you?

153
00:05:48,007 --> 00:05:49,380
没有 没有 完全没有
Uh, no. No, no, no, no, no.

154
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:50,660
很抱歉 教授
I'm so sorry, Professor.

155
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:52,240
你说的话永远不会让我觉得无聊
Nothing you could say would ever bore me.

156
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:53,258
我尊敬你
I revere you.

157
00:05:53,258 --> 00:05:55,722
实际上 去年万圣节我扮成了你
I actually went as you last year for Halloween.

158
00:05:55,722 --> 00:05:58,460
好吧 这是我的手机 别怪我妹妹
Okay, it's my phone. Don't blame my sister.

159
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,500
切尔西 回头再给你回电话
Hey, Chelsea. Gonna have to call you back.

160
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:03,660
-我不信 你闭嘴 -闭嘴
- Shut up! Shut up! - Shut up!

161
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:05,460
不好意思 切尔西的朋友
Excuse me, Chelsea's friend.

162
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:07,540
你看起来不像是我的学生
Y-You don't look like one of my students.

163
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:09,400
谢谢 你嘴真甜
Oh, thank you! That is so sweet.

164
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:11,800
不是 你为什么来这里
No. Why are you here?

165
00:06:11,940 --> 00:06:13,760
我今天有个重要的工作面试
Oh, I have a really big job interview today,

166
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:15,460
我需要有人检查下我写的...
and I need someone to look over what I wrote for my --

167
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:17,660
我们走了 我带她出去 很抱歉
Yeah, we're going. I'm taking her out. I am so sorry.

168
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,440
干嘛 是他问的 你太没礼貌了
What? He asked. You're being rude.

169
00:06:24,943 --> 00:06:26,658
-太暴露了 -出去
- Very revealing. - Get out.

170
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,860
克莱尔 很高兴你给我打了电话
Claire, I'm so glad you called.

171
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:31,440
我们之前怎么从来没聚过
How come we've never done this before?

172
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:32,780
因为我们两家是世仇
Because we were born into a feud.

173
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:35,150
血仇世家哈特菲尔德和麦科伊 鲨鱼队和喷气机队
Hatfields and McCoys, the Sharks and Jets,

174
00:06:35,150 --> 00:06:38,328
衣柜疯子和衣柜笨蛋
the -- the closet lunatic and the closet idiot.

175
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:40,660
-顺便说一句 很遗憾你爸爸去世了 -谢谢
- By the way, I'm really sorry about your dad. - Thanks.

176
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,680
你知道他为什么让人把骨灰寄给我爸爸吗
Do you have any idea why he had his ashes sent to my dad?

177
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,999
-也许是为了把他逼疯吧 -效果拔群
- Probably to drive him bonkers. - Well, it's working.

178
00:06:46,999 --> 00:06:48,441
他知道了会很高兴的
That would've made him happy.

179
00:06:49,020 --> 00:06:51,780
咱们约定吧 永远不要像他们一样
Let's make a pact -- to never be like them.

180
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:52,547
我同意
I am in.

181
00:06:52,547 --> 00:06:55,320
我们是男性统治行业中的两个女人
We are two women in a male-dominated industry.

182
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,700
我们该帮助彼此
We should help each other.

183
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:58,800
实际上 你知道有谁会做
Actually, do you have any sources

184
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,300
古董菠萝把手吗
for antique pineapple knobs?

185
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,099
我们在做殖民地系列
We're doing this whole colonial line --

186
00:07:02,099 --> 00:07:03,620
拉兹罗肯定知道
Ooh, I bet you Lazlo would know.

187
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:04,458
他是我们的首席设计师
He's our lead designer.

188
00:07:04,458 --> 00:07:07,435
大家都知道拉兹罗是谁 他是个传奇
Everybody knows who Lazlo is. He's a legend.

189
00:07:07,435 --> 00:07:09,460
也是我唯一一个有价值的员工
Yeah, and my only employee worth a damn.

190
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:11,339
机器人工人 那才是未来
Robot workers. Now, that's the future.

191
00:07:11,339 --> 00:07:13,180
对啊 它们从不休息
Right! They work 24/7,

192
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:14,999
而且你不用给它们买生日蛋糕
and you don't have to buy them a birthday cake.

193
00:07:14,999 --> 00:07:16,600
机器人变得更像人类时
Yeah, and as they become more human,

194
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,540
你就可以说 你 来我办公室
you can be like, "Hey, you, come into my office",

195
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:20,940
-然后"吃干抹净"了它们 -是啊
- and then you just go to town on them. - Yeah.

196
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:24,880
什么鬼
What the hell?

197
00:07:25,063 --> 00:07:27,220
汽修店怎么了
What happened to the bodyshop?

198
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:28,560
我们只是保留了招牌
Oh, we just kept the sign.

199
00:07:29,079 --> 00:07:31,298
马里奥不在了吗
Oh, uh, so -- so no M-Mario?

200
00:07:31,536 --> 00:07:33,366
是啊 我们是艺术家联盟
Mnh-mnh. We're an artist collective.

201
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:34,760
吉莉安玩毛线艺术
Jillian works in yarn,

202
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,540
芒福德用乐高做雕像 邓肯是画家
Mumford sculpts with Lego, Duncan is a painter.

203
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,560
我能给你们写首诗吗
May I write you a poem?

204
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:40,740
你在逗我吗
Are you kidding me?

205
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:41,978
我就跟你说有这职业
I told you it was a career.

206
00:07:41,978 --> 00:07:45,875
你有没有见过我儿子
Um, any chance that you have, uh, seen my son?

207
00:07:45,940 --> 00:07:46,799
没有 抱歉
No, I'm sorry.

208
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:48,880
好吧 他昨晚来了这附近
Oh, okay. He -- He was around here last night.

209
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,940
他貌似跟这附近的一个姑娘走了
He apparently went off with a girl from this neighborhood.

210
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,420
从那以后我们再也没能联系上他
We just haven't been able to reach him since.

211
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:53,379
你知道那姑娘的名字吗
Do you know the girl's name?

212
00:07:53,379 --> 00:07:55,382
不知道 像是个拉丁名字
No. Uh, something Latin-y.

213
00:07:55,524 --> 00:07:58,860
你怎么了 你以前还是拉丁男孩呢
What happened to you? You used to be Latin-y.

214
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,080
能描述一下她的外貌吗
Can you describe her?

215
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:02,180
棕色头发 高颧骨
Brown hair, high cheekbones --

216
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:05,000
他要做什么 用乐高把她做出来吗
What is he gonna do, build her out of Legos?

217
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:09,160
万万没想到会有如此神效
Huh, that is surprisingly effective.

218
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:11,900
等等 我认识那姑娘
Wait a minute. I know that girl.

219
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:14,260
她好像在一家小蛋糕店工作
I think she works at a cupcake shop.

220
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,460
真棒 在哪里
Great. Where is it?

221
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,380
我不确定是哪家 因为这里有四家
Well, I'm not sure which one because we have four.

222
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:19,600
一家叫"小蛋糕!" 加了个感叹号
There's Cupcakes! With an exclamation point,

223
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,398
卖素食小蛋糕的"小淡糕"
there's vegan cupcakes at Cupfakes,

224
00:08:21,398 --> 00:08:23,760
"狗蛋糕"是买给狗狗的宠物小蛋糕店
there's Pupcakes, which sells cupcakes for dogs,

225
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,120
还有"瑞克的录像机修理店"
and then there's Rick's VCR Repair.

226
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:27,160
那家的小蛋糕最好吃
Oh, they make the best cupcakes.

227
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,080
白痴麦克斯 害我们得在
Stupid Max, forcing us to eat our caviar

228
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,880
在如此普通的周五早上吃鱼子酱
on a regular Friday morning.

229
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:33,740
我根本无法享受鱼子酱的美味
I can't even enjoy the symphony of flavors,

230
00:08:33,740 --> 00:08:35,820
或它在我口中融化的感觉
or the -- or the way that it melts in my mouth.

231
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:38,360
那你干嘛不随便喝口剩下的酒咽下去得了
Why don't you just wash it down with whatever wine's left.

232
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:39,100
对呀 干嘛不呢
Yeah, why don't I.

233
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:40,000
-干杯 -干杯
- Cheers. - Cheers.

234
00:08:42,115 --> 00:08:43,526
果然不出所料 你知道吗
Mmm, and, of course, you know what?

235
00:08:43,580 --> 00:08:44,360
这俩绝配
It pairs perfectly.

236
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:48,040
我不敢相信我吃着一生最棒的一顿饭
I-I cannot believe I'm having one of the best meals of my life

237
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,540
却没有庆祝任何事情
and we're not even celebrating anything.

238
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:50,720
谢谢了 麦克斯
Yeah, thanks, Max!

239
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:52,540
-谢谢了麦克斯 -谢你全家啊麦克斯
- Thank you, Max. - Thank you, Max.

240
00:08:57,167 --> 00:08:59,020
小卡 有没有可能
Cam, is it -- is it -- is it possible

241
00:08:59,020 --> 00:09:00,861
我们其实真的很享受
that we're actually enjoying ourselves

242
00:09:00,861 --> 00:09:02,100
麦克斯是对的
and -- and that Max was right?

243
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:03,800
或许我们真的总在延迟享受
Maybe we do defer enjoyment.

244
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:05,799
那些没用完的飞行里程
All those unspent frequent flyer miles,

245
00:09:05,799 --> 00:09:07,600
那我等了好久才穿的靴子
the boots that I have waited so long to wear

246
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:09,041
穿时已经过时了
that they're no longer in style,

247
00:09:09,041 --> 00:09:10,520
还有那些冲浪板
the -- the -- the surfboards

248
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:11,800
咱们从来没用过
that we've never used because

249
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:14,140
因为要等到最完美的冲浪日子
it just "had to be the perfect beach day".

250
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,860
你要干嘛
What are you doing?

251
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:18,700
-米奇尔 -我要点了它
- Mitchell... - I'm lighting it.

252
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:19,920
-不 -我要点了它
-No! - I'm lighting it!

253
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:22,160
不 这是印有名字的婚礼蜡烛
No, that is our monogrammed wedding candle,

254
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:23,580
我们要把它留到特殊场合
and we're supposed to save it.

255
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,540
什么场合呢 小卡
For what, Cam?

256
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:27,100
-我不知道 -你不知道
- I don't know! - You don't know.

257
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:28,080
-我不知道 -你不知道
- I don't. - You don't know.

258
00:09:29,886 --> 00:09:30,916
看
Ohh...look at it.

259
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:34,040
好像闻到了永恒的爱
Smells like eternal love.

260
00:09:35,691 --> 00:09:36,576
好吧
Aww...oh. O-kay.

261
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:39,580
为什么你老在我办公室
Why are you always in my office?

262
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:40,980
我在这儿效率最高
I do my best work in here.

263
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:43,460
我在试着进入他的思路
I've been trying to get into his head.

264
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:45,300
我甚至还买了他最喜欢的午饭
I even brought his favorite lunch --

265
00:09:45,660 --> 00:09:47,000
鸡尾酒虾 波本酒
shrimp cocktail and bourbon.

266
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,060
那不过是你每天午餐吃的东西啊
Or that's just what you have for lunch every day.

267
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,740
这也是厄尔从我那里偷学走的
That's another thing Earl stole from me!

268
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:52,920
-你发现什么了 -首先
- What did you find out? - First of all,

269
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:54,920
雪儿不知道有关骨灰的任何事
Shirl doesn't know anything about the ashes.

270
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:55,999
其次 我们不会
And second, we're not

271
00:09:55,999 --> 00:09:57,578
像你俩一样不和
gonna be a part of your little feud anymore.

272
00:09:57,578 --> 00:09:59,760
-我们会成为朋友 -她耍你呢
- We're gonna be friends. - She's playing you!

273
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:00,940
-不会 -我问你
- No... -Let me ask you a question.

274
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:03,580
你告诉她我们投标贝尔蒙特花园了吗
Did you tell her we're bidding on Belmont Gardens?

275
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:04,500
没 怎么了
No. Why?

276
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:07,280
因为15分钟前 我接到个电话
Because 15 minutes ago, I got a phone call

277
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:08,820
说突然之间
saying just out of the blue,

278
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:12,160
"衣柜衣柜衣柜衣柜"公司和我们竞标
Closets Closets Closets Closets is bidding against us.

279
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:14,020
她看了你的提案了吗
Did she see your proposal?

280
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:16,100
看了 爸 我肯定
Yes, Dad! I'm quite sure she

281
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:17,980
她在我去卫生间的时候翻了我的包
rifled through my bag when I was in the bathroom.

282
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:18,640
你去卫生间了吗
You went to the bathroom?

283
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:21,040
-你咋不直接把公司送她呢 -天啊
- Why don't you just give her the company?! - Oh, God.

284
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:25,120
-你瞧 番茄酱 -这说明什么
- Bingo! Ketchup! - What does that prove?

285
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:26,260
她午餐是不是吃了番茄酱
Did she have ketchup for lunch?

286
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,080
她的确吃了薯条
She had... French fries.

287
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:29,579
证据确凿
There's your smoking gun.

288
00:10:29,579 --> 00:10:30,841
玛格丽特 我需要
Margaret? I'm gonna need

289
00:10:30,841 --> 00:10:32,833
薯条和番茄酱来进入雪儿的思路
fries and ketchup to get in Shirl's head.

290
00:10:32,833 --> 00:10:34,506
不不 雪儿不会这么做的
No! No, Shirl wouldn't have done this.

291
00:10:34,506 --> 00:10:35,287
坏消息
Um, bad news.

292
00:10:35,287 --> 00:10:37,760
我们好不容易找到的那些菠萝把手
Uh, we finally tracked down those pineapple knobs,

293
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:40,040
但刚被买下 是衣柜
but they were all just bought up by Closets...

294
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:40,880
-不 -衣柜
- No. - Closets...

295
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:41,860
不 玛格丽特
No, Margaret!

296
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:42,980
衣柜衣柜公司
...Closets Closets.

297
00:10:45,618 --> 00:10:46,740
雪儿玩了我
Shirl screwed me.

298
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:47,680
你知道你要怎么做吗
You know what you have to do?

299
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,300
你得戳她的痛处
You've got to hit her where it hurts.

300
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:51,200
她最珍视什么
What does she value most?

301
00:10:51,686 --> 00:10:52,826
拉兹罗
Lazlo.

302
00:10:52,980 --> 00:10:53,940
我觉得你没明白
I don't think you understand

303
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:56,163
这对我来说有多丢人
how humiliating that was for me.

304
00:10:56,163 --> 00:10:58,280
这尴尬可能会缠着我一辈子
There are parts of me that will never uncringe.

305
00:10:58,280 --> 00:10:59,920
天啊
Oh, my God!

306
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,179
我打断了无聊的故事而已
So I interrupted some boring story.

307
00:11:02,179 --> 00:11:03,147
阿尔文·费诺曼博士
Dr. Arvin Fennerman

308
00:11:03,147 --> 00:11:05,680
是一个大奖的两次获得者
is a two-time Vanderkoff Grant winner --

309
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:07,220
一次是哲学一次是几何学
one for philosophy and one for geometry.

310
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:08,300
你不能就这么...
You can't put him into a box

311
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:09,580
-因为 -你能不能看下我的文章
- because... - Could you please just read my sample?

312
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:11,560
这个工作对我来说很重要
This job is important to me.

313
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:13,540
这是我有一份真正工作的唯一机会
This is my one shot at a real career.

314
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:15,400
好 我读 但"真正工作"吗
Fine, I'll read it. And "Real career"?

315
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,460
我看过这个诺普公司的吧
I've seen this NERP business.

316
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:19,280
妮可·罗丝玛丽·佩奇看起来就有病
Nicole Rosemary Page seems bonkers.

317
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,180
她不是因为食人事件出事了吗
Didn't she get in trouble for cannibalism?

318
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:23,980
没有 事实证明没有法律禁止
No. Turns out there are no laws against

319
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:25,440
吃自己的阑尾
eating your own appendix,

320
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:27,360
而且这样有助于保持身材
and it does help with fine lines.

321
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:29,080
但她是个成功的典范
But she's a success story.

322
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:30,880
童星 邦德女郎
Child star, bond girl,

323
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,500
在钱全被方氏骗局卷走前还是独立甜心
indie darling before she lost all her money to a Fonzie scheme.

324
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:36,220
-你说的是庞氏骗局吧 -很遗憾 还真不是呢
- Don't you mean Ponzi scheme? - Sadly, no.

325
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:38,740
然后出于绝望 她成立了诺普
So, out of desperation, she invented NERP,

326
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:40,940
接下来突然之间就成为商业帝国
and next thing you know -- boom! Empire.

327
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,560
我只想成为伟大事业的一部分
I just want to be a part of something great.

328
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,039
说实话
Well, if I'm being honest,

329
00:11:44,039 --> 00:11:45,720
你写得还不错
your writing sample's actually pretty good.

330
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:46,799
真的吗 谢谢
Really?! Thank you.

331
00:11:46,799 --> 00:11:48,135
天啊 费诺曼博士
Oh, my God. It's Dr. Fennerman.

332
00:11:48,135 --> 00:11:50,193
别思考 别呼吸 头低下
Don't think, don't breathe, keep your head down. O-kay.

333
00:11:54,140 --> 00:11:54,540
你们好
Hello.

334
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:57,480
不好意思 你好 博士
Sorry! Hello, Doctor.

335
00:11:57,780 --> 00:11:58,700
要下坐吗
Would you like down sit?

336
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:02,160
-什么鬼 -太好了你人 艾丽克斯
- What? - Kind, that's very you of, Alex.

337
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:06,680
再和我说下 你为什么在我的班上
Um...tell me again, why were you in my class?

338
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:08,140
我有个很重要的面试
I have a very big interview

339
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,980
是和妮可·罗丝玛丽·佩奇 她刚刚...
with Nicole Rosemary Page, and she was just --

340
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:11,920
你知道她是个江湖骗子吧
Ugh! You know she's a snake oil salesman, right?

341
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:12,860
我知道
Yes, I know.

342
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:14,840
人们一直抱怨腹泻
People complain about the diarrhea all the time,

343
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:15,820
但减肥不就...
but that is the point.

344
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:17,779
她的科学就是一派胡言
Her science is utter nonsense.

345
00:12:17,779 --> 00:12:20,267
什么能给你能量的宇宙贴纸
I mean, space stickers that give you energy,

346
00:12:20,267 --> 00:12:22,220
能吸收无线网信号的水晶
and crystals that absorb Wi-Fi,

347
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:23,980
1200块一双的袜子 有没有搞错
and seriously -- $1,200 socks?

348
00:12:23,980 --> 00:12:25,640
做袜子的羊毛出自只吃寿司的羊
Those sheep eat nothing but sushi.

349
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:27,600
-我们说完没有 -神奇的是 没有
- Are we done here? - Surprisingly, not.

350
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,380
这或许听起来很疯狂 但
This might sound crazy, but...

351
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:32,460
我要和你结婚
I'm going to marry you.

352
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:33,140
什么
What?!

353
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:35,597
抱歉 你第一次和活生生的女生说话吗
I'm sorry, first time talking to a real girl?

354
00:12:35,597 --> 00:12:38,220
不 听我说 我也搞不懂
No, l-l-listen. I-I-I don't get it.

355
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:40,180
其实我也吓到了
Frankly, it boggles the mind,

356
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:41,400
但自从刚才遇见你
but I've been running

357
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:45,164
我在脑袋里运算了数十种可能的情形
dozens of probability scenarios in my head since we met,

358
00:12:45,164 --> 00:12:47,203
最终结果都是我们
and-and they all end with us...

359
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:48,953
在一起了
...together.

360
00:12:48,953 --> 00:12:51,620
我这辈子也听过不少很瞎的搭讪词 但...
I have heard some lame pickup lines in my day, but --

361
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:52,499
那种词我也有不少存货
I have plenty of those.

362
00:12:52,499 --> 00:12:54,620
你是神经电流吗
Are you a neuro-electrical current

363
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:56,560
因为你整天都在我脑袋里跑来跑去
because you've been running through my mind all day?

364
00:12:56,571 --> 00:12:57,999
但这次不一样
But th-th-that's not what this is.

365
00:12:57,999 --> 00:13:00,480
咱俩肯定会在一起 海莉·邓菲
This is going to happen, Haley Dunphy.

366
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:02,100
-你怎么知道我的名字 -我什么都知道
- Ew, how do you know my name? - I know everything.

367
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,858
而且你的通行证上面有名字
Also, your pass has your name written on it.

368
00:13:04,858 --> 00:13:06,160
我觉得我要晕过去了
I think I'm gonna pass out.

369
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:09,340
我把我的联系方式空投到你电话上了
Right, I've just air-dropped my contact info to your phone.

370
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,678
要不你就按一下接受
You just tap to accept it.

371
00:13:11,678 --> 00:13:14,580
我是不会"要"的
Uh, yeah, not gonna...tap that.

372
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:15,440
我认为你会的
I think you will.

373
00:13:16,507 --> 00:13:18,720
海莉 宇宙中有许多力
Haley, there are forces in the universe

374
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:20,000
是我们无法理解的
that we don't understand...

375
00:13:20,504 --> 00:13:23,834
可测却无法解释的力
measurable forces that...can't be explained,

376
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:26,180
但没人能否认它的存在
but cannot be denied...

377
00:13:27,221 --> 00:13:29,415
咱俩之间就是这样
and that's-that's what this is.

378
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:33,660
我也无法理解 但我知道它是真实存在的
I don't get it, but...I know that it's real.

379
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,859
这也太智障了吧
That was so dumb!

380
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:41,493
什么 哪里智障 你才智障
What? No, it wasn't. You're-you're dumb.

381
00:13:41,619 --> 00:13:44,200
会烙印进你脑海的 我已在你脑海之中
That's gonna stick. I'm-I'm in your head.

382
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,060
-好吧 -等着瞧
- Okay. - You'll see.

383
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,855
行行行 兄弟 走人时尽量走得帅一点
Sure, buddy. Now try and walk away cool.

384
00:13:46,855 --> 00:13:48,764
-我会的 -那好
- Oh, I will. - Okay.

385
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:55,180
我们本来在这里亲热
We were standing right here making out.

386
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:56,820
突然间他说"我去去就回"
All of a sudden, he said, "I'll be right back",

387
00:13:57,100 --> 00:13:58,540
之后我就没见过他了
and that was the last I saw of him.

388
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:00,420
各位 我的休息时间结束了
You guys, my break is over,

389
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:01,400
我希望你们能找到他
but I hope you find him.

390
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:02,780
谢谢你的帮助
Thank you for your help,

391
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:04,890
顺带一提 小蛋糕很好吃
and the cupcakes are delicious, by the way.

392
00:14:04,890 --> 00:14:07,390
-那是给狗狗吃的 -不是吧
- Those are for dogs. - Oh, no.

393
00:14:07,390 --> 00:14:09,880
-菲尔 你没事吧 -没事没事
- Ay, Phil, are you okay? - Yeah, yeah.

394
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:12,801
我很肯定卢克是有什么充分的理由
I'm sure there's a perfectly reasonable explanation

395
00:14:12,801 --> 00:14:15,700
才会放弃和女孩亲热
why Luke would abandon a make-out sesh.

396
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:16,360
不 根本没有
No, there isn't.

397
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:18,220
邓菲家的男人永远不会那样做
A Dunphy man would never do that.

398
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,590
我们会临阵脱逃 被蜘蛛吓跑
We walk away from fights, we walk away from spiders,

399
00:14:21,590 --> 00:14:24,480
但永远不会离开身上有糖霜味的可爱女孩
but never a super-cute girl who smells like frosting!

400
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:25,520
你得保持乐观
You have to stay positive.

401
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:28,820
高级家具店的附近从来不会出什么事
Nothing bad ever happens this close to a Pottery Barn.

402
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:30,100
我一直在假装勇敢
I've been putting on a brave face

403
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:31,560
来压制内心的黑暗
to squash the darkness inside of me,

404
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:32,620
但万一发生了最坏的状况呢
but what if the worst has happened?

405
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:33,880
我该怎么和克莱尔说 我不说
How will I tell Claire? I won't.

406
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,760
我得用枕头捂死她免得她伤心
I'll have to smother her with a pillow to spare her the pain,

407
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,000
但那样杰就会失去女儿
but then Jay will have lost a daughter.

408
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,120
我得把他也捂死
I'll have to smother him, too.

409
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,839
那两只枕头是成套的 成了我的惯用手法
That's two pillows from the same set. It's a pattern.

410
00:14:39,839 --> 00:14:42,704
-我被警察盯上了 -给老娘打起精神来
- The police are after me! - Get ahold of yourself!

411
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:44,638
你手也太重了
What the hell?

412
00:14:44,638 --> 00:14:46,968
不是我 你瞧 我手还没落下去呢
It wasn't me. Look, I'm still cocked!

413
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:47,780
是只鞋
It was a shoe.

414
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:49,940
等等 这是
Wait, that's...

415
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:51,340
是卢克的鞋
that's Luke's.

416
00:14:53,180 --> 00:14:55,460
卢克 你没事
Luke! You're okay!

417
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:57,400
我被困在屋顶上了
I got stuck on the roof.

418
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,160
这下我放心了
I'm so relieved!

419
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:01,200
我不用捂死你妈了
I don't have to kill your mother!

420
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:04,520
原来卢克当时要上厕所
Turns out, Luke had to go to the bathroom.

421
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:05,940
有人告诉他厕所在楼上
Someone told him it was upstairs,

422
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:07,500
他就一路上到了屋顶
so he walked all the way up to the roof

423
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:08,660
不小心把自己反锁在屋顶了
and locked himself out.

424
00:15:08,792 --> 00:15:10,900
他电话没电了 街上音乐声太大
His phone was dead, and he-he lost his voice

425
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:12,560
他大声喊得嗓子也哑了
trying to scream over the street musicians.

426
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:15,960
我松了口气 跑上去狠狠亲了他一口
I was so relieved, I ran up there and gave him a big kiss.

427
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:17,240
歌洛莉亚
Gloria!

428
00:15:18,820 --> 00:15:20,280
我们被困住了
Hi. We're stuck.

429
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:22,340
你上来帮我们开个门行吗
Could you pop on up and open the door?

430
00:15:23,143 --> 00:15:24,451
邓菲家男儿啊
Dunphy men.

431
00:15:28,798 --> 00:15:30,179
你好 拉兹萝
Hello, Lazlo.

432
00:15:30,229 --> 00:15:33,566
-发音是"拉兹罗" -我就是这么念的啊
- It's pronounced "Lazlo". - That's what I said.

433
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,200
谢谢你来见我们
Thank you so much for meeting with us.

434
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:37,000
你有没有考虑我们的提议
Have you had a chance to consider our offer

435
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,060
加入普利切特衣柜
to join Pritchett's Closets?

436
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:40,680
我有兴趣 但我有张条件单
I'm intrigued, but I have a list of demands.

437
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:43,060
好的 当然
Ah, yes, of course.

438
00:15:43,399 --> 00:15:44,429
条件有
We have, uh...

439
00:15:45,076 --> 00:15:47,360
"两个装满白色口香糖的绿松石碗
...uh, "Two turquoise bowls of white Chiclets,

440
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:49,559
有地漏的空办公室"
an empty office with a drain in the floor..."

441
00:15:49,559 --> 00:15:52,418
-"尖叫室"是什么 -这还用解释吗
- What's a "Scream room"? - I think that's self-explanatory.

442
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:53,220
普里契特
Pritchett!

443
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:54,320
厄尔闺女
Girl Earl!

444
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:58,194
你居然想从我这挖走拉兹罗
You're actually trying to poach Lazlo from me?

445
00:15:58,500 --> 00:15:59,880
我还以为我们是朋友
I thought we were friends.

446
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:02,200
本来是 可你买走了所有菠萝门把手
We were, and then you bought all my pineapple knobs.

447
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,980
-买来送你的 -什么
- As a gift! - What?

448
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,920
-我发到你那去了 -是吗
- I had them sent to you. - You did?

449
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:06,740
别被她蛊惑
Don't listen to her.

450
00:16:06,780 --> 00:16:08,740
这都是她变态计划的一部分
This is all part of some sick plan.

451
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:10,460
偷看克莱尔的提案
Stealing Claire's proposals,

452
00:16:10,460 --> 00:16:12,820
送来厄尔的骨灰让我闹心
Earl's urn to get in my head.

453
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:14,520
但你的小伎俩是不会成功的
But your little games are not gonna work.

454
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,460
是的 你要怎么解释
Yeah. Yeah, how do you explain

455
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:18,920
我提案上面的番茄酱 薯条妹
the red ketchup stains on my proposal, French Fries?

456
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,480
我从不沾番茄酱
I never use ketchup.

457
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:22,760
我吃薯条跟与拉兹罗亲密时一样
I like my fries the way I like my Lazlo...

458
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:24,580
光着来
undressed.

459
00:16:25,338 --> 00:16:26,660
小低低
Twiddle-Dee.

460
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:28,600
你们俩的关系好复杂啊
You guys have a really complicated relationship.

461
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:30,540
你那红色的污渍是什么
And what's that red stain?

462
00:16:34,723 --> 00:16:36,194
鸡尾酒虾酱
Shrimp cocktail sauce, uh-oh.

463
00:16:36,483 --> 00:16:37,518
爸
Dad!

464
00:16:37,518 --> 00:16:38,740
-雪儿 -省省吧
- Shirl... - Save it.

465
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:41,360
我们本来可以当好朋友呢 但算了吧
We could have been friends. Well, forget it.

466
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:42,540
要战便战
Game on.

467
00:16:43,876 --> 00:16:45,028
雪儿
Shirl...

468
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:46,460
她有什么诡计
What is she up to?

469
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:49,759
没有 你的神经病阴谋论害我损失了朋友
No, no. Your crazy conspiracy theories just cost me a friend.

470
00:16:49,759 --> 00:16:50,751
我还以为我终于找到了
I thought I'd finally found

471
00:16:50,751 --> 00:16:52,512
一个业界盟友
an -- an ally in this industry,

472
00:16:52,512 --> 00:16:55,836
一个与我... 共登山巅的伙伴
somebody to... to climb the hill with.

473
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:58,300
共登山巅 天啊 就是这个
Up the hill! Oh, my God! That's it!

474
00:16:58,480 --> 00:17:01,180
不行 不许你现在跟我来顿悟这招
No, no, you do not get to have an epiphany right now!

475
00:17:01,180 --> 00:17:02,550
我要被你气炸了
I am furious at you!

476
00:17:02,550 --> 00:17:05,391
我的回答是 我愿意
The answer is...yes.

477
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:08,160
很多人说诺普
People say that NERP

478
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,901
不过是骗钱的玩意
is nothing more than a con job,

479
00:17:09,901 --> 00:17:12,932
脑残女演员的刷脸骗钱项目
a cash-grab vanity project from a kooky actress.

480
00:17:14,180 --> 00:17:15,587
抱歉 这是在提问吗
Oh, I'm sorry. Was that a question?

481
00:17:15,587 --> 00:17:17,580
-不是 -那就好
- No. - Oh, okay.

482
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:18,100
但是
But...

483
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:19,220
真是这样吗
is it true?

484
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:21,920
-他们总不跟我说真话 -"他们"是指谁
- They don't tell me things. - Who's "They"?

485
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:25,120
但我不觉得诺普是个生意
See, I don't see NERP as, like, a business.

486
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:28,280
-这更像是种... -生活方式 我也是
- It's more, like, a kind of... - Like a way of life! Me too!

487
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:31,580
迪士尼创办人华特·迪士尼曾发想过
Walt Disney once... envisioned...

488
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:33,460
一个魔法世界...
a magical world...

489
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:35,576
但别人都说他是疯子
...and people told him he was mad.

490
00:17:35,576 --> 00:17:37,741
他们称那地方为"华特蠢地"
They called it "Walt's Folly."

491
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:39,980
-但你知道后来那里变成哪儿了吗 -迪士尼乐园
- But you know what that place became? - Disneyland.

492
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:43,215
-我没有在问你 -对不起
- That was not a question. - Oh, I -- I'm sorry.

493
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:48,260
那地方成了迪士尼乐园
That place is Disneyland.

494
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:51,620
真的假的 不是吧 完全没猜到
What?! That's crazy. Didn't see it coming.

495
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:53,240
我希望把我公司
I want to turn NERP

496
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:56,578
变成下一个迪士尼 脸书 特斯拉 肉毒针
into the next Disney-Facebook-Tesla-Botox.

497
00:17:56,578 --> 00:18:00,021
能改变世界 变成通向未来的道路
It's a world changer. It's a road map to the future.

498
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,400
这是个问题啊
That was a question!

499
00:18:05,424 --> 00:18:06,997
算了 听我说
Alright, listen.

500
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:10,520
我很喜欢你写的样品文章 真心的
I really liked your writing sample, it's true.

501
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:12,720
但是...
But...

502
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,868
我们有很多应征者
...we have a lot of candidates

503
00:18:14,868 --> 00:18:18,100
有丰富的经验 更有名气的父母
with more experience and famous-er parents,

504
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:18,820
所以...
so...

505
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:20,000
飞走吧 小鸟
fly away, little birdie.

506
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:24,400
啪嗒 啪嗒 啪嗒
Flap. Flap, flap.

507
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:27,480
好吧 谢谢
Okay, thank you.

508
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:31,380
妮可
Nicole?

509
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:35,160
你和我 咱俩肯定能行
You and me -- this is gonna happen.

510
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:35,900
你说什么
Excuse me?

511
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:39,340
宇宙中有许多力是我们无法理解的
There are forces in the universe that we don't understand.

512
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:41,740
它们无法被解释 但它们的存在也无法否认
They can't be explained, but they cannot be denied,

513
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:43,180
而我们也是一样
and that is what this is.

514
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:46,360
我无法理解 但我知道这是真实存在的
I don't -- I don't get it, but I know that it's real.

515
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:48,080
天啊
Oh, my God!

516
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:51,000
我也是这么跟那些喷子说的
That is just what I said to all of those haters

517
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,530
就是那些说我的水晶能量贴纸
who told me that my crystal energy stickers

518
00:18:53,530 --> 00:18:55,517
并不能改善结肠健康的人
did not improve your colon health.

519
00:18:55,681 --> 00:18:56,460
神经病
Uh! Crazy.

520
00:18:56,460 --> 00:18:57,460
是能有效的 只要...
They do if you, you know...

521
00:18:57,460 --> 00:18:58,040
是啊
Yeah.

522
00:18:58,440 --> 00:19:01,140
所以下周一早上我们能再见吗
So, um, does that mean that I will see you Monday morning?

523
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:02,420
周二吧
Let's make it Tuesday

524
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:04,580
因为我周一喜欢在漂浮缸里待着
'cause I like to spend Mondays in a flotation tank.

525
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:10,480
年轻时 我们沿着这条路爬到这棵老橡树
As young men, we'd hike this path up to an old oak tree,

526
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:13,320
我们一起动脑想着怎么征服衣柜世界
where we'd brainstorm how to conquer the closet universe.

527
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:16,480
我们当年傻傻地以为自己什么都懂
We foolishly thought that we knew everything back then.

528
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:20,040
但我乐观地希望我这些年来有学到几件事
But hopefully, I've learned a few things through the years.

529
00:19:22,974 --> 00:19:26,210
比如 仿佛没有明天般认真活在当下
Like, live today as if there is no tomorrow.

530
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:30,540
弥补过去的错误何时都不晚
it's not too late to right past wrongs,

531
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:33,880
当一切都在走下坡时 要向上看
and when things are looking down, look up...

532
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:37,720
抓住你永远以为自己不会尝试的机会
...or take chances you never imagined you would.

533
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:48,700
"你个傻逼娘炮 我就知道你会做
"You stupid softy, I knew you'd do it.

534
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:51,240
你有没有有试着搞点煽情的啊
Did you try to do something special?

535
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:53,120
是不是日落时分
Was it at sunset?

536
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,940
就是日落时分 对吧
It was at sunset, wasn't it?

537
00:19:57,720 --> 00:19:59,520
娘们 我赢了
Sucker. I win.

538
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:01,560
咱们地狱再见"
See you in hell."

539
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:06,480
我拭目以待
I look forward to that.

540
00:20:24,077 --> 00:20:24,866
这太爽了
Whoo! Ohh, this is amazing!

541
00:20:24,866 --> 00:20:27,349
对啊 我们好几年前就该这么做了
I know! We should have done this years ago.

542
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:28,900
我有点冷啊 你是不是也有点冷
Whoa. I'm a little cold. Are you a little cold?

543
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:30,580
是啊 我还没被冻僵的部位的确有点冷
Yeah, the parts of me that I can still feel sure are. Yeah.

544
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:32,880
看看那些下班在回家路上的废柴
Oh, look at those suckers on their way home from work.

545
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:34,760
祝生意场狗咬狗愉快啊
Enjoy the rat race!

546
00:20:35,181 --> 00:20:38,011
-别忘了要纳税啊 -对啊
- Don't forget to pay your taxes! - Yeah!

547
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:41,300
你有没有读到那个... 恐龙鱼的文章
Hey, did you see the story about that, um, dinosaur fish?

548
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:44,175
文章说它的头... 是个蛇的头之类的
It said it had the head of... a head of a snake or something.

549
00:20:44,175 --> 00:20:45,698
有 有16排牙齿嘛
Yeah, 16 rows of teeth, uh-huh.

550
00:20:47,660 --> 00:20:49,700
你觉得我们从水下看像两只海豹吗
Hey, do you think that we look like seals from underneath?

551
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:51,420
米奇尔 我们这是在干嘛
Mitchell, w-what are we doing?

552
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:54,933
我们在干... 我们这是在享受人生啊
What are we... We're living our lives, is what we're doing.

553
00:20:54,933 --> 00:20:56,755
是啊 我知道 我只是问问
Yeah, but I, uh, I'm just asking,

554
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:59,500
但想象是不是比现实做更有意思啊
but was imagining it more fun?

555
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,460
好歹更暖和
Well, it was warmer.

556
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:03,440
你知道吗 我很喜欢期待一件事情
You know, I like looking forward to things.

557
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:05,400
女歌手卡莉·赛门的名曲是"预期"
Carly Simon's big hit was "Anticipation",

558
00:21:06,260 --> 00:21:07,800
不是"还记得我们做过的那些牛逼事"吗
not "Remember That Cool Thing We Did".

559
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:08,876
我有个主意
Hey, I have an idea.

560
00:21:08,876 --> 00:21:12,235
我们就回去 买一瓶永远没机会开的酒
L-Let's go back, we'll buy a bottle of wine that we'll never open

561
00:21:12,235 --> 00:21:14,000
一根永远没机会点的蜡烛
and a candle that we'll never light,

562
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,440
-然后今天就收工 -这主意听起来很赞
- call it a day, huh? - That sounds wonderful.

563
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:17,020
好了 但你别再碰我脚了
Okay, but stop touching my feet.

564
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:17,640
我没碰你脚
I didn't touch you.

565
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:19,361
我没碰你的脚
I didn't touch you.

566
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:20,401
-你没... -我没碰你
- You didn't... - I didn't touch you.

567
00:21:20,401 --> 00:21:22,612
-恐龙鱼 是恐龙鱼 -恐龙鱼 恐龙鱼
- Dinosaur fish! Dinosaur fish! - Dinosaur fish! Dinosaur fish!

568
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:26,140
米奇尔 米奇尔 不许你留下我一个人
Mitchell! Mitchell, do not leave me alone!
